Question:How web works?
Ans: When we type a url inside a web browser it sends request to a dns server to get the ip address of the web page.After getting ip address a http request is sent to the server in question which also sends the web page in the form of packets to the client. these packets get combined again at our browser and we can see the webpage. These packets are part of http protocal which are rapped inside tcp protocal which is mainly responible for combining these packets and which in itself is packed inside the layer of ip protocal which is responsible for sending the packets to the right location.